poetry:l3-y6@claude-opus-5-5.text:
Forgotten loves sigh in rain;
the bare tree's boughs are hushed:
summer sang, and sings no more.

poetry:pantoum@claude-opus-5-5.text:
The summer sang in me, and sings no more.
Ghosts tap the glass and listen in the rain;
I have forgotten lips I kissed before.
No lad at midnight turns to me again.

Ghosts tap the glass and listen in the rain;
The winter tree knows not what birds have flown.
No lad at midnight turns to me again;
It knows how silent all its boughs have grown.

The winter tree knows not what birds have flown;
I have forgotten lips I kissed before.
It knows how silent all its boughs have grown:
The summer sang in me, and sings no more.

poetry:l3-y6@claude-fable-5-2.text:
I forget what lips I kissed;
A winter tree, I know
My summer sings no more.

poetry:shakespearean-sonnet@gpt-6-luna.text:
I have forgot what lips I kissed, and where,
And why, what arms beneath my head have lain;
Till morning; now the rain is full of ghosts
That tap the glass and sigh against the pane.

They listen at the glass for my reply;
For unremembered lads, a quiet pain
Stirs in my heart; they will not turn to cry
At midnight, nor return to me again.

The winter tree stands silent as before;
Which birds have vanished cannot now be known;
Its boughs hold silence, nothing more,
And there it stands, through winter, still alone.

I cannot say what loves have come and gone;
I only know summer sang, then was done.

poetry:heroic-couplets@gpt-6-luna.text:
I've lost what lips I kissed, and where, and why,
And which arms held my head till morning light.

The rain is full of ghosts that tap and sigh;
They listen at the glass for my reply.

I cannot say what loves have come and gone,
Yet feel a quiet pain for every one.

Which birds have left, the winter tree can't say;
Its boughs are quieter than yesterday.

I know that summer sang in me before;
It sang a little while, and sings no more.

poetry:l3-y5@claude-opus-5-5.text:
My loves, unrecalled,
are ghosts in the rain;
summer sings no more.

poetry:l4-y2@claude-opus-5-5.text:
Loves go;
rain sighs;
boughs know
song dies.

poetry:l5-y1@claude-opus-5-5.text:
Loves fade;
rain sighs;
boughs hush;
summer's
gone.

poetry:l3-y5@claude-fable-5-2.text:
I forget each kiss;
My winter boughs know
Summer sings no more.

poetry:l3-y7@claude-fable-5-2.text:
I forget the lips I kissed;
Like a winter tree, I know
Summer sings in me no more.

poetry:l3-y5@claude-haiku-5-5.text:
I forget my lovers,
yet still I mourn them;
my summer sang. It's mute.
